+# Organiser announcement supplied by the user
+
+Recorded 2026-09-30 from the message pasted into the project conversation.
+Sender: Xinghao Zhu, NVIDIA. Message header: Tuesday, 29 September, 1:48 PM;
+the pasted header does not state a time zone. This is a summary of user-supplied
+source text, not an independent email or website retrieval.
+
+The message announces that challenge submissions and leaderboards are live, and
+points teams to the challenge website for the Submission Kit and evaluation
+requirements. It asks teams to submit early and improve from leaderboard results.
+
+It describes the released accelerated RL framework as training dexterous and
+whole-body manipulation policies in approximately two hours on one L40S GPU.
+That claim does not establish training time or memory requirements on the local
+RTX 5080. FlashCHORD's pinned README separately specifies 48 GiB for full training.
+
+Teams may submit five times each week, with unlimited submissions during the
+final three days. The weekly reset and exact start of the final window are not
+given in the message.
+
+The message names NVIDIA Omniverse Discord's #v2d-challenge channel, with track
+and general-question threads, and says an FAQ exists and will be updated. It
+provides no FAQ or Discord invite URL in the pasted text.
+
+The participant webinar is 7 October 2026 at 11 AM Pacific, with access details
+to follow. The roadmap records that as 8 October at 05:00 in Sydney. Nothing in
+this announcement authorizes local execution, installation, uploads or messages.
